  "slug": "depth-compartment-bb23",
  "summary": "Recent preprints show that transcriptomic and chromatin readouts depend on cell composition, scoring rules, marker definitions and donor structure.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is that omics readouts are conditional on the compartment, cell composition, scoring rule, marker definition and donor structure from which they are drawn. Decoupled transcript scoring of efferocytosis after ischaemic stroke, assessed across 38 datasets, finds clearance signals bounded by cell composition and time. Endometriosis GWAS cell-state prioritization shifts with marker definition, and chromatin accessibility in endometrial biopsies places stromal regulatory context in view. A sequence model conditioned on interferon-beta-stimulated monocyte snapshots predicts the expression response to an unseen stimulus but not stimulus-dependent genetic effects, which defines a boundary on transfer. In cortical GABAergic Patch-seq neurons, channel expression reinforces rather than compensates for dendritic conductance load. Across these preprints, interpretation is tied to the specific context in which each readout was obtained, and the non-coding DNA framework and ImmunoTwin screens extend this view to regulatory and perturbational settings.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
